<title>GREECE: Greek Diekat turnover up 86pct in Jan-May.</title>
<headline>Greek Diekat turnover up 86pct in Jan-May.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Construction company Diekat said in a statement that its turnover rose 86 percent to 2.6 billion drachmas ($9.5 million) in the first five months of the year from 1.4 billion in the same period in 1996.</p>
<p>Its orderbook is currently valued at 14 billion drachmas.</p>
<p>Shareholders approved the distribution of a cash dividend per share of 145 drachmas, up from 138 drachmas for fiscal 1995, it said.</p>
<p>Diekat's pretax profit rose to 1.4 billion drachmas in 1996 from 1.2 billion in 1995 on turnover of 7.95 billion drachmas compared to 7.74 billion in 1995, it added.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4 ($ = 272.2 Greek Drachmas)</p>
